815	# Local setup
816	
817	Requirements: Node 22 or newer, pnpm, Docker.
818	
819	```bash
820	pnpm install
821	pnpm run stack:up      # infra, migrations, build, all five apps
822	pnpm run stack:down    # stop apps and infra, keep the data
823	pnpm run stack:reset   # drop the data and start fresh
824	```
825	
826	`stack:up` creates `.env` on first run through `scripts/make-local-env.sh`. The file holds throwaway local values, is gitignored and must never be committed. App logs go to `tmp/logs/`.
827	
828	To run a second copy of the stack on the same machine, set `PORT_OFFSET` and `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME` before the first `stack:up`.
829	
830	## Environment variables
831	
832	| Name | Used by |
833	|---|---|
834	| `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME`, `PORT_OFFSET` | docker compose, `scripts/make-local-env.sh` |
835	| `NODE_ENV` | all apps. Not kept in `.env`, where it would leak into `next build`; `stack:up` sets `production` when it starts the apps |
836	| `DB_HOST`, `DB_PORT`, `DB_USERNAME`, `DB_PASSWORD`, `DB_DATABASE` | `booking`, `room`, migrations |
837	| `REDIS_HOST`, `REDIS_PORT` | `booking`, `worker` |
838	| `NATS_PORT` | docker compose |
839	| `NATS_URL` | `gateway`, `booking`, `room`, `worker` |
840	| `GATEWAY_PORT`, `WEB_ORIGIN` | `gateway` |
841	| `WEB_PORT`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` | `web` |
842	make-local-env.sh
843	stack-down.sh
844	stack-reset.sh
845	stack-up.sh
